  "status": "published",
  "title": "Potting Bench",
  "summary": "A mud-room-height workbench for repotting, with a slatted lower shelf and a peg rail for trowels.",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedHours": 6,
  "imageUrl": "/projects/potting-bench.jpg",
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Cut the two end panels from 3/4 in plywood, each with a flat top and a notch toward the bottom for the lower shelf apron. Mark the top edge at a comfortable 36 in working height.",
    "Cut the top slats and the two aprons, then screw the aprons across the tops of both ends with the top surface flush.",
    "Screw the slats across the aprons with a 1/4 in gap between them so water and soil drain off the working surface.",
    "Fit the lower shelf on the notch, and screw it to the end panels with the shelf boards set 1/2 in apart.",
    "Add a back trim piece and a peg rail drilled for six steel hooks for trowels and snips.",
    "Drive screws through the top into the aprons on the back edge, then sand all end-grain and round over every working edge.",
    "Seal with two coats of outdoor deck sealer so the bench survives water and soil."
  ],
